},{"content_hash":"ca777a46886d1aa2b36ca8ce20ed24d2f686df1812675b40f23bc6a2ce44b53d","event_uuid":"98592bb6-d35d-4f9c-9827-203bc2f56e0e","position":{"commit_sha":"7ce4db430492043215794adf66f2ff4d1398dedb","position":"1787090380781181001-98592bb6-d35d-4f9c-9827-203bc2f56e0e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8ebfc3a4f508563074490dfd5c916e3959e3977508100157732937b78ca2a43b","event_uuid":"5fe5a16b-769f-4588-aadf-70fbb3175ced","position":{"commit_sha":"7f00d61f60dc446f398e16cff780ef0c747d9475","position":"1787090884693077609-5fe5a16b-769f-4588-aadf-70fbb3175ced"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"9d376b2f74fa744b3a04a795633f1ee899699decad41559a13e767c2a85521c9","event_uuid":"0c0636d6-36e4-49cf-92c6-add2b0cf77d4","position":{"commit_sha":"dc8fd219a5e2a35900aeb67ee5ba32003c59b1d2","position":"1787092450972553001-0c0636d6-36e4-49cf-92c6-add2b0cf77d4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a231e4651fa69849ed28157c0cec07501db2ccf03712ff72860d0ff1dd99ba9d","event_uuid":"5bc509e9-01cb-44e0-9111-d86a7a4fd02a","position":{"commit_sha":"d3c6701fe211c83f666df8a342d4d641f55b4eaf","position":"1787092600437836001-5bc509e9-01cb-44e0-9111-d86a7a4fd02a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"78f4cd30b69d1ae583ddd16015e6ca9170f0d303424933aa00572b8923617ac9","event_uuid":"cb47615b-aa31-4ebf-a544-0d0cc2ba71d9","position":{"commit_sha":"96e3bb769447a0903f71b1682465a4930adc7679","position":"1787092956235024850-cb47615b-aa31-4ebf-a544-0d0cc2ba71d9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787081605647076001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7941dcdc-3a9f-465b-9382-a9696123aa5f","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8"},{"link_uuid":"5fe5a16b-769f-4588-aadf-70fbb3175ced","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2130-7d59-e5a5-4119"},{"link_uuid":"cb47615b-aa31-4ebf-a544-0d0cc2ba71d9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5465-ef01-c33c-4d47"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe ownership-direction gate `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` (created by slice C1,\nticket 29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8) and the existing field-consumption gate\n`scripts/check_config_reads.py` are only useful if they run on every change through a\nportable trigger that needs NO CI provider, with CI as a mirror. Today\n`scripts/check_config_reads.py` runs ONLY as a standalone \"Config-read gate\" step in\n`.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` (wrapped in the ee2a if-present tree-skew guard),\nand `scripts/check_config_ownership.py` runs nowhere. rebar must work with diverse CI\nproviders or no CI provider, so the primary trigger must be the portable local `make lint`\npath.\n\n## Outcome\nThe `lint` target in `Makefile` runs BOTH `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and\n`python scripts/check_config_reads.py`. Because CI already runs `make lint` (the\n`_SHARED_GATE_SIGNATURES` \"make lint\" entry, asserted present in `_build-and-test.yml` by\n`test_ci_workflow_parity.py`), CI runs both gates THROUGH that one `make lint` step — so\nthe now-redundant standalone \"Config-read gate\" workflow step is REMOVED (its coverage\nmoves to `make lint`), which also eliminates the double-run that would occur if both the\nstandalone step and `make lint` invoked the field-consumption gate.\n\n## Design decisions (resolving the double-run / lost-skip-guard tension)\n1. **Single source = `make lint`.** Both gate invocations live in exactly one place: the\n   `lint` target. CI inherits them via its existing `make lint` step; no CI step invokes\n   either gate directly, so neither gate runs twice per job.\n2. **The ee2a if-present guard is no longer needed and is dropped with the standalone\n   step.** That guard let a Gerrit patchset predating `check_config_reads.py` pass. Under\n   `make lint` the equivalent protection is INHERENT: CI runs the PATCHSET's own `Makefile`,\n   and a patchset predating this slice has a `Makefile` without these invocation lines, so\n   `make lint` simply does not run the gates — no missing-file failure, and the gate\n   re-enforces on rebase and on every post-merge change. This is strictly MORE portable\n   (operation-linked to `make lint`, not CI-only).\n3. **The existing CI-wiring guard is re-anchored, not duplicated.**\n   `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_heldout.py::test_ci_wires_the_gate` currently\n   greps `_build-and-test.yml` for `check_config_reads.py`; since the invocation moves out\n   of the workflow into `make lint`, that test is updated to assert the `Makefile` `lint`\n   target wires the field-consumption gate (it would otherwise red on the removed step).\n\n## Plan\n1. Add `python scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and `python scripts/check_config_reads.py`\n   to the `lint` target in `Makefile`.\n2. Remove the standalone \"Config-read gate\" step (and its ee2a if-present guard) from\n   `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml`.\n3. Re-anchor `test_check_config_reads_heldout.py::test_ci_wires_the_gate` to assert the\n   `Makefile` `lint` target contains `check_config_reads.py`.\n4. Extend `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py`: assert the `Makefile` `lint` target\n   contains BOTH gate invocations AND that CI still runs `make lint` (the existing shared\n   signature) — so removing either gate line from the Makefile, or removing `make lint`\n   from the workflow, fails the parity check (fed synthetic edited copies).\n\n## Testing (RED -> GREEN)\n- A parity test asserts that removing the ownership-gate invocation from a synthetic copy\n  of the Makefile `lint` target fails the check, and likewise for the field-consumption\n  gate; and that a synthetic workflow copy dropping `make lint` fails (so CI cannot silently\n  stop running the gates it inherits).\n- `make lint` executes both gates and remains green on the current tree (with C1's\n  populated legacy-exception set).\n- The gates run under `make lint` with NO CI provider present (portable path), proving the\n  trigger is operation-linked, not CI-only.\n- The re-anchored `test_ci_wires_the_gate` passes against the Makefile.\n\n## Dependency\nDepends on slice C1 (ticket 29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8), which creates\n`scripts/check_config_ownership.py` and its legacy-exception set; AC3's greenness on the\ncurrent tree requires C1's exception set. The `depends_on` edge C2->C1 is recorded.\n\n## Compatibility / rollback\nWiring-only; no product-code change. Rollback restores the standalone workflow step,\nreverts the Makefile additions, and restores the original `test_ci_wires_the_gate` anchor.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The `Makefile` `lint` target executes both the ownership-direction gate\n  (`scripts/check_config_ownership.py`) and the field-consumption gate\n  (`scripts/check_config_reads.py`); CI runs both through its existing `make lint` step, and\n  the standalone \"Config-read gate\" workflow step is removed (no double-run).\n- [x] The workflow-parity tests fail if either gate invocation is removed from the Makefile\n  `lint` target, or if `make lint` is removed from the workflow.\n- [x] `test_check_config_reads_heldout.py::test_ci_wires_the_gate` is re-anchored to the\n  Makefile and passes.\n- [x] `make lint` runs both gates with no CI provider present (portable/no-CI path) and\n  remains green on the current tree.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"Makefile","reason":"Wire both config gates into the portable lint target (single source)."},{"path":".github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml","reason":"Remove the now-redundant standalone Config-read step; CI runs both gates via make lint."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","reason":"Assert make lint wires both gates + CI keeps make lint; fail if dropped."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_config_gate_wiring_heldout.py","reason":"NEW held-out red-proofs: synthetic-removal teeth for the parity invariant."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_heldout.py","reason":"Re-anchor test_ci_wires_the_gate from the workflow to the Makefile (gate moved to make lint)."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_check_criteria_vocabulary.py","reason":"Stub the two new lint-target gate scripts in the make-lint sandbox so it still reaches the vocabulary guard."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","29a9-3cf7-3ded-42d8"],["parent","aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4"],["relates_to","2130-7d59-e5a5-4119"],["relates_to","5465-ef01-c33c-4d47"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"aabf-d89e-d05a-45c4","parent_status_uuid":"51015418-dee0-424d-9104-f2502ecd6d37","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"735b-cec9-fd08-4851","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-04 S7.2 — Wire ownership + field-consumption gates into make lint + CI parity","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["056cd497-301f-479c-9348-cdac970c6bc3","40cf58b4-f3de-497f-ac7e-a9cc824a1a33","51015418-dee0-424d-9104-f2502ecd6d37","50fff37c-6692-4616-bce7-f55809507e98","294c78a9-de9e-4c2f-acef-ae40d307c9a3","e05d90ad-8720-41c8-add2-07a3ca3984ba","98592bb6-d35d-4f9c-9827-203bc2f56e0e","5fe5a16b-769f-4588-aadf-70fbb3175ced","0c0636d6-36e4-49cf-92c6-add2b0cf77d4","5bc509e9-01cb-44e0-9111-d86a7a4fd02a","cb47615b-aa31-4ebf-a544-0d0cc2ba71d9"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787092956235024851,"uuid":"58a3e4f8-0c3a-4fab-8f23-ce0e39451c78"}